#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introdución"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This module allows to configure certain parts of the desktop search and the "
"Nepomuk semantic desktop. More information about the Nepomuk semantic "
"desktop can be found at the <ulink url=\"http://nepomuk.kde.org/\">Nepomuk "
"homepage</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"Este módulo permite configurar certas partes da busca no escritorio e do "
"escritorio semántico Nepomuk. Pode atopar máis información sobre o "
"escritorio semántico Nepomuk na <ulink url=\"http://nepomuk.kde.org/"
"\">Páxina web do Nepomuk</ulink>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic Settings"
msgstr "Configuración básica"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:40
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The basic settings page allows to enable or disable the semantic desktop "
#| "and desktop search systems."
msgid ""
"The basic settings tab allows to enable or disable the semantic desktop and "
"desktop search systems."
msgstr ""
"A páxina de configuración básica permítelle activar ou desactivar os "
"sistemas de escritorio semántico e de busca no escritorio."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:42
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "There are two checkboxes:"
msgid "There are three checkboxes:"
msgstr "Hai dúas opcións:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Enable Nepomuk Semantic Desktop</guilabel> Enabling the Nepomuk "
"semantic desktop means that the Nepomuk services are running. These services "
"provide metadata/annotation storage (files can be tagged or rated in "
"&dolphin; for example) but also desktop search which can be used through the "
"&kde; runner or again &dolphin;."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Activar o escritorio semántico Nepomuk</guilabel> Activalo fará "
"que os servizos de Nepomuk se executen. Estes servizos proporcionan almacéns "
"de metadatos e anotacións (por exemplo para etiquetar ou cualificar os "
"ficheiros en &dolphin;) e tamén buscas no escritorio que se poden usar no "
"runner de &kde; ou en &dolphin;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:47
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<guilabel>Enable Strigi Desktop File Indexer</guilabel> Enabling the "
#| "Strigi desktop file indexer means that the Nepomuk Strigi service is "
#| "started in addition to the standard services already running. The Strigi "
#| "service will run through all files in the configured folders (see below) "
#| "and extract metadata from them (such as title or artist on music files or "
#| "even simple things like the creation date). This metadata is then exposed "
#| "through the desktop search just like the manual annotations mentioned "
#| "earlier."
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Enable Nepomuk File Indexer</guilabel> Enabling the nepomuk file "
"indexer means that the file indexer service is started in addition to the "
"standard services already running. The file indexer service will run through "
"all files in the configured folders (see below) and extract metadata from "
"them (such as title or artist on music files or even simple things like the "
"creation date). This metadata is then exposed through the desktop search "
"just like the manual annotations mentioned earlier."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Activar o indexador de ficheiros do escritorio Strigi</guilabel> "
"Activar isto fará que o servizo Strigi do Nepomuk se inicie ademais dos "
"servizos estándar que xa se estean a executar. O servizo Strigi executarase "
"por todos os ficheiros nos cartafoles que se configurase (ver embaixo) e ha "
"extraer os seus metadatos (como o título ou o artista dos ficheiros de "
"música ou a data de creación do ficheiro). Estes metadatos expóñense na "
"busca do escritorio igual que as anotacións manuais mencionadas antes."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Enable PIM Data Indexer</guilabel> This option has to be checked "
"to allow full text search in &kmail;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right of <guilabel>Enable Nepomuk Semantic Desktop</guilabel> you can "
"click on <guilabel>Details...</guilabel> and a dialog will inform you on the "
"status of the KDE metadata store: how many files are indexed and the size of "
"the store."
msgstr ""
"Á dereita de <guilabel>Activar o escritorio semántico Nepomuk</guilabel> "
"está o botón  <guilabel>Detalles…</guilabel> que serve para mostrar un "
"diálogo que o ha informar do estado do almacén de metadatos de KDE: cantos "
"ficheiros se indexan e o tamaño do almacén."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Under the <guilabel>Enable Strigi Desktop File Indexer</guilabel> "
#| "checkbox the current status of the Strigi service is shown. The service "
#| "has four normal operation states:"
msgid ""
"Under the <guilabel>Enable Nepomuk File Indexer</guilabel> checkbox the "
"current status of the file indexing service is shown. The service has four "
"normal operation states:"
msgstr ""
"Baixo da casiña <guilabel>Activar o indexador de ficheiros do escritorio "
"Strigi</guilabel> móstrase o estado actual do servizo Strigi. Este ten catro "
"estados normais de operación:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>File indexer is idle</guilabel> - The file indexer is currently "
"not working and waiting for an event to trigger an update (an event can be a "
"newly created file or a changed file or a timeout for the recurring full "
"check)"
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>O indexador de ficheiros está ocioso</guilabel> Indica que o "
"indexador non está a traballar e que está a agardar que algún acontecemento "
"inicie unha actualización (un acontecemento pode ser que se cree ou que se "
"modifique un ficheiro, ou esgotar o tempo límite da comprobación periódica)."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<guilabel>Strigi is currently indexing files in folder foobar</guilabel> "
#| "- The file indexer is currently running though all files in folder foobar "
#| "and analyzes new or changed files."
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Indexing files in folder foobar</guilabel> - The file indexer is "
"currently running though all files in folder foobar and analyzes new or "
"changed files."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Strigi está a indexar os ficheiros que hai no cartafol lolailo</"
"guilabel> Indica que o indexador de ficheiros está a traballar nos ficheiros "
"do cartafol lolailo analizando os ficheiros novos ou modificados."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<guilabel>Checking file system for new files</guilabel> - The file "
#| "indexer is currently performing its recurring check for new files in all "
#| "index folders. This check is intended to find files that were not caught "
#| "through normal file system monitoring."
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Scanning for recent changes in files for desktop search</guilabel> "
"- The file indexer is currently performing its recurring check for new files "
"in all index folders. This check is intended to find files that were not "
"caught through normal file system monitoring."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Estase a comprobar a existencia de ficheiros novos no sistema de "
"ficheiros</guilabel> O indexador de ficheiros está a facer unha comprobación "
"recursiva á procura de novos ficheiros por todos os cartafoles indexados. "
"Esta comprobación debería atopar ficheiros que non se detectasen mediante a "
"vixilancia normal do sistema de ficheiros."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>File indexer is suspended</guilabel> - The file indexer has been "
"suspended, &ie; it is in a paused state. This can either be triggered by the "
"user or due to low disk space or a laptop being in a power-saving state. In "
"the two latter cases the indexer will resume once the reason for the "
"suspension has been resolved."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>O indexador de ficheiros está suspendido</guilabel> Suspendeuse o "
"indexador de ficheiros, &ie; está en pausa. Isto pode acontecer a petición "
"do usuario, debido a ter pouco espazo no disco ou a ser un portátil nun "
"estado de aforro de enerxía. Nestes dous casos continuará de novo o traballo "
"cando o motivo da suspensión desapareza."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Apart from the normal operation states the Strigi service can have an "
#| "erroneous state. There are two possibilities:"
msgid ""
"Apart from the normal operation states the indexer service can have an "
"erroneous state. There are two possibilities:"
msgstr ""
"Á parte dos estados normais de traballo o servizo Strigi pode estar nun "
"estado de erro, para o cal hai dúas posibilidades:"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<guilabel>Strigi service failed to initialize, most likely due to an "
#| "installation problem.</guilabel> - This should rarely occur that means "
#| "that a mandatory plugin could not be loaded. This can be due to an "
#| "installation problem (missing dependency) or due to a faulty setup of the "
#| "&kde; plugin system."
msgid ""
"<guilabel>File indexing service failed to initialize, most likely due to an "
"installation problem</guilabel> - This should rarely occur that means that a "
"mandatory plugin could not be loaded. This can be due to an installation "
"problem (missing dependency) or due to a faulty setup of the &kde; plugin "
"system."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Fallou o inicio do servizo Strigi, posibelmente debido a un "
"problema de instalación.</guilabel> Isto significa que non foi posíbel "
"cargar un complemento obrigatorio; posibelmente se deba a un problema coa "
"instalación (dependencia que falta) ou a unha mala configuración do sistema "
"de complementos d &kde;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any other error means a communication problem with the service. These errors "
"are produced by the &DBus; subsystem and need to be evaluated case by case."
msgstr ""
"Calquera outro erro significa que houbo un problema de comunicación do "
"servizo. Estes erros débense ao &DBus; e deben avaliarse caso por caso.."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indexing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab allows to select the files and folders that are to be analyzed by "
"the file indexer explained above. By default Documents, Audio, Images and "
"Videos are selected here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:92
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "This tab allows to fine tune the files and folders that are to be "
#| "analyzed by the Strigi file indexer explained above. The left panel "
#| "allows to select and de-select folders that should be searched for files "
#| "to be analyzed. By default the home folder and all subfolders are "
#| "analyzed. By simply unchecking a folder it can be excluded. It is also "
#| "possible to include a subfolder of an excluded one by checking it again. "
#| "This allows a rather fine selection of the folders to be analyzed."
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Customize Folders</guibutton> button to select and de-"
"select folders that should be searched for files to be analyzed. By default "
"the home folder and all subfolders are analyzed. By simply unchecking a "
"folder it can be excluded. It is also possible to include a subfolder of an "
"excluded one by checking it again. This allows a rather fine selection of "
"the folders to be analyzed."
msgstr ""
"Nesta lingüeta poderá axustar os ficheiros e cartafoles que ha analizar o "
"indexador. No panel da esquerda poderá escoller os cartafoles onde se deben "
"buscar os ficheiros para analizar; por omisión analízanse o cartafol persoal "
"e todos os subcartafoles pero se desmarca calquera cartafol hase excluír. "
"Pode incluírse un subcartafol dun cartafol excluído marcándoo, deste xeito "
"poderá facer un axuste bastante preciso dos cartafoles para analizar."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The right panel allows to define exclude filters. The filenames of all "
#| "files found in the configured folders will be matched against these "
#| "filters. Only if none of them matches the file will be analyzed. This is "
#| "very helpful to exclude log and backup files and the like."
msgid ""
"Clicking the <guibutton>Advanced</guibutton> button allows to define exclude "
"filters using the mime type or the name of a file. The mime types and names "
"of all files found in the configured folders will be matched against these "
"filters. Only if none of them matches the file will be analyzed. This is "
"very helpful to exclude log and backup files and the like."
msgstr ""
"No panel da dereita pódense definir filtros para excluír. Os nomes dos "
"ficheiros que se atopen nos cartafoles configurados hanse cotexar con estes "
"filtros e só aqueles que non casen con ningún han analizarse. Isto é moi "
"útil para excluír ficheiros de rexistro, copias de seguranza e cousas á "
"maneira."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Removable media handling</guilabel>: Nepomuk can index files on "
"removable devices like USB keys or external hard-disks for fast desktop "
"searches. By default no files are indexed. Here this behaviour can be "
"changed to one of two options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Index files on all removable devices</guilabel> - Files on "
"removable media are indexed as soon as the medium is mounted. Caution: this "
"does not include media which have been rejected via the second option"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Ask individually when newly mounted</guilabel> - The user will be "
"asked to decide if files on the newly mounted medium should be indexed or "
"not. Once decided Nepomuk will not ask again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backup"
msgstr "Copia de seguranza"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab you can decide to make a backup of all data that could not be "
"restored otherwise. This includes manually created tags, ratings but also "
"statistical data. No backup is done as default so you need to decide what "
"you want to do. You have two possibilities: automatic backups and manual "
"ones."
msgstr ""
"Nesta lapela pode decidir facer unha copia de seguranza de todos os datos "
"que non se poderían recuperar doutro xeito, incluíndo etiquetas creadas á "
"mao, cualificacións e datos estatísticos. Por omisión non se fai copia de "
"seguranza ningunha, polo que terá que decidir o que quere facer. Ten dúas "
"posibilidades: copias automáticas ou manuais."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Backups"
msgstr "Copias de seguranza automáticas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First choose the <guilabel>Backup Frequency</guilabel>: this is set to "
"<guilabel>Disable Automatic Backups</guilabel> but you can choose "
"<guilabel>Daily Backup</guilabel> or <guilabel>Weekly Backup</guilabel>. "
"Then set the <guilabel>Backup Time:</guilabel> to anything convenient for "
"you using the spinbox: you can set the hour and minutes and the day of the "
"week for weekly backups. Finally you can set a limit for the number of "
"backup files using <guilabel>Max Number of Backups:</guilabel>. This will "
"ensure you do not waste disk space with the backup files and only the N last "
"files will be kept, N being the number you set there, 10 as default."
msgstr ""
"Primeiro escolla a <guilabel>Frecuencia da copia de seguranza</guilabel>: "
"está como <guilabel>Desactivar as copias de seguranza</guilabel> pero pode "
"escoller <guilabel>Copia diaria</guilabel> ou <guilabel>Copia semanal</"
"guilabel>. Logo escolla a <guilabel>Hora á que facer a copia:</guilabel> cun "
"valor axeitado mediante o selector: pode escoller a hora e os minutos e o "
"día da semana se a copia é semanal. Finalmente pode definir un límite ao "
"número de ficheiros de copia de seguranza mediante o <guilabel>Número máximo "
"de copias que se van manter:</guilabel>, deste xeito pode garantir que non "
"se malgaste espazo no disco en ficheiros de copia de seguranza e que só os "
"últimos N ficheiros se han conservar, sendo N o número que indique aquí, 10 "
"por omisión."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your automatic backups are saved locally in the following directory: "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$KDEHOME/share/apps/nepomuk/backupsync/backups/"
"</filename>."
msgstr ""
"As copias automáticas gárdanse localmente no directorio <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$KDEHOME/share/apps/nepomuk/backupsync/backups/</"
"filename>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tools"
msgstr "Ferramentas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Manual Backup...</guilabel> You can also perform manual backups. "
"Manual backups will be saved in your chosen location, as a file. Click on "
"<guilabel>Manual Backup...</guilabel> and a wizard will guide you. You first "
"need to point to the location of the backup file. Enter a full valid path in "
"the field or use the file dialog to point to a file."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Facer unha copia de seguranza manual..</guilabel> Tamén pode facer "
"as copias no momento que queira. As copias manuais gardaranse no lugar que "
"escolla como un ficheiro. Prema o botón <guilabel>Facer unha copia de "
"seguranza manual</guilabel> e guiarao un asistente: primeiro debe indicar o "
"lugar onde gardar o ficheiro coa copia. Indique unha rota completa ou use o "
"diálogo de ficheiros para indicar un ficheiro."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can create a new file in the folder of your choice and then point to "
"this new file."
msgstr "Pode crear un ficheiro novo onde escola e logo indicar este."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then click on the <guibutton>Next</guibutton> button and the dialog should "
"report that the backup has been done."
msgstr ""
"Logo prema o botón <guibutton>Seguinte</guibutton> e o diálogo debería "
"informar de que se fixo a copia."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Restore Backup...</guilabel> If you want to later restore your "
"backup, use this button and follow the wizard. The backup will be merged "
"into the local Nepomuk database."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel>Restaurar unha copia de seguranza…</guilabel> Se quere recuperar a "
"copia use este botón e o seguinte asistente. A copia hase xuntar na base de "
"datos local do Nepomuk."

